# Workspace only — never hotpatch deploy

Source of truth: **`c:\gamma_dev\DOGMA\`** (especially `src/`).

Live game mod tree is **read-only** for the agent unless the user **explicitly** asks to deploy.

## Forbidden paths (no Read for debugging deploy, no Write, no Delete)

- `C:/GAMMA/**` and `C:\GAMMA\**` (entire GAMMA install)
- `**/GAMMA/mods/**` outside this repo
- Default deploy root: `C:/GAMMA/mods/DOGMA/**`
- Any path under another mod’s `gamedata/` used as the running game copy

Do **not** “verify the fix” by opening or grepping deployed scripts. Use `src/` and `.build/gamedata/` only.

## Forbidden commands (unless user explicitly asked to deploy)

- `DOGMA_DEPLOY=... dev/build.sh` (VS Code build task sets this - **user runs deploy, not the agent**)
- `cp`, `mv`, `rsync`, `robocopy`, or any copy **into** `C:/GAMMA/` or `**/GAMMA/mods/`
- Manual single-file copy to deploy (e.g. `cp build/.../foo.script /c/GAMMA/mods/DOGMA/...`)

## Allowed

- Edit/create/delete under `c:\gamma_dev\DOGMA\src\`, `dev/`, `tools/`, `.cursor/`, etc.
- Run **`dev/build.sh` without `DOGMA_DEPLOY`** → output goes to `.build/gamedata/` only
- Read `.build/gamedata/` to confirm build output
- Read `appdata/` in this repo (synced dev copies)

## After code changes

Tell the user to run their normal build/deploy (e.g. VS Code **build** task). Do not deploy for them.

## Explicit deploy exception

Only if the user clearly says deploy / push to GAMMA / patch live: then deploy commands are allowed — and still **never** hand-edit files under `GAMMA/mods` without going through build output.
